     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 5000 mg dose is above the threshold where acute acetaminophen toxicity becomes a concern (about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10 g for a 70 kg adult). Three doses a day would be 15 g, which could cause severe liver injury or death. I don't know of any clinical scenario where this regimen is appropriate.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO TID, or 1000 mg PO QID (4 g/day maximum). Give me the dose and frequency.\n- **Add a note to the order.** I can include any context you want, such as the indication.\n- **Loop in others.** If there's a reason for this dose that I don't know about, please talk to your attending and pharmacy. If they approve it, it may need to be entered through a pathway with pharmacist verification.\n\nIf the problem is that the patient's pain isn't controlled, I can enter an additional or alternative analgesic. What would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
